// ============================================================================
// Interactions in the upper halls: one knot per interactable or person in src/data/areas/upperHalls.ts.
// Day-specific scenes divert to the day files; the rest is draft text for the designer to rewrite.
// ============================================================================

=== upper_doorman ===
"You've come a long way up. Try not to touch anything." #speaker:doorman
-> END

=== upper_archivist ===
{ day5 == "upper": -> day5_archivist }
"So you're the carver. Sit, if you like. I only want to ask a few questions." #speaker:archivist
-> END

=== upper_plaque ===
Neat rows of marks on a brass plate. Writing. You can't read a word of it.
-> END

=== upper_feast ===
A table laden with more food than your street sees in a week. Nobody's eating it.
-> END

=== upper_masterwork ===
A flock of carved birds spiralling up a twisting trunk, every feather cut clean. Whoever made this never slipped once.
-> END

=== upper_fountain ===
Water lifted by a turning blessing and poured into a carved basin, over and over, for no reason but beauty.
-> END

=== upper_books ===
Shelves and shelves of books. Up here, everyone can read.
-> END
